This package uses source format 3.0 (quilt). The orig tarball must not
contain the debian/ directory.

Install the build dependencies:

  sudo apt install build-essential debhelper dh-python gettext python3 lintian

From a git checkout of the matching upstream version:

  rm -rf /tmp/kblueproximity-orig
  mkdir -p /tmp/kblueproximity-orig
  git archive --format=tar --prefix=kblueproximity-2.2.3/ HEAD \
    | tar -x -C /tmp/kblueproximity-orig
  rm -rf /tmp/kblueproximity-orig/kblueproximity-2.2.3/debian
  tar -C /tmp/kblueproximity-orig --owner=root --group=root --sort=name \
    -czf ../kblueproximity_2.2.3.orig.tar.gz kblueproximity-2.2.3

Then build with:

  dpkg-buildpackage -us -uc -S
  dpkg-buildpackage -us -uc -b
  lintian -I ../kblueproximity_2.2.3-1.dsc ../kblueproximity_2.2.3-1_all.deb

uscan (debian/watch) expects an upstream GitHub tag such as v2.2.3.

After the ITP bug is filed, add "(Closes: #nnnnnn)" to debian/changelog
and change the distribution from UNRELEASED to unstable.
